-- 05_registry_pq.cov
--
-- AUDIT FIXTURE, ERC-8231 post-quantum key registry via `registry` keyword.
--
-- Purpose : verify ERC-8231 surface synthesis (Sprint 35.b).
--
-- Auto-synthesized fields :
--   keys        : map<address, pq_key>
--   registered  : map<address, bool>
--
-- Auto-synthesized views :
--   is_registered(account) returns bool
--   key_of(account) returns pq_key
--   algorithm_id() returns uint256, returns 1 = Dilithium-5 (FIPS 204)
--
-- Auto-synthesized actions :
--   register(pk: pq_key), open-access ; caller registers their own key
--   revoke(), caller clears their own slot only
--
-- Auto-synthesized events :
--   KeyRegistered(indexed account, pq_key)
--   KeyUpdated(indexed account, pq_key), reserved for Sprint 35.c
--   KeyRevoked(indexed account)
--
-- Auto-synthesized errors :
--   NotRegistered, AlreadyRegistered
--
-- V0.9.0 audit warnings :
--   * `update_key(new_pk, sig)` (PQ-signed key rotation) is reserved in
--     the synthesizer's name conflict list but NOT YET EMITTED. Sprint
--     35.c will add it once `pq_signed` guards integrate with stdlib
--     synthesis. Auditors should NOT expect this method on V0.9.0 ABIs.
--   * `register` is open-access. The caller registers their OWN address.
--     There is no "register on behalf of" path, by design.
--   * `revoke` clears the caller's own slot only. There is no admin
--     override, by design (matches ERC-8231 spec).
--
-- Helper-contract bridge :
--   `pq_key` operations dispatch to MockedPQVerifier on Sepolia/Aster.
--   The Mocked* helper does NOT perform real Dilithium verification,
--   it returns a deterministic dummy proof. See
--   docs/v0.9/known-acceptable-risks.md.

registry AuditKeyRegistry {
}
